ng  the elderly and those living with  disabilities many confined to their  homes are now left starving and alone  crystal commansing reports on a unique  program designed to help ukraine's most  vulnerable  sitting in her wheelchair svetlana  savchenko smiles warmly it's been a long  night she explains four rockets hit  nearby  and she hasn't slept  my home that is hardcover region but  there is no one  her cat busia her only companion her  husband and son died years ago twice a  month the volunteer from harkief hub  swings by and drops off a small plastic  bag with a few items  there's not much inside yet she's  grateful  her parting words lead to tears  take care of your mothers if you have  one  mothers are your guardian angels elderly  people are extremely vulnerable in this  war especially in areas under heavy  shelling like kharkiv the world bank  estimates the number of ukrainians  living below the national poverty line  could reach 70 percent this year it was  18 percent in 2021  every week volunteers deliver an average  of 1500 small parcels some drivers have  had their cars struck with shrapnel  still they get behind the wheel  local businesses are supporting the  effort along with unicef but the  coordinator of the harkief hub says  there are too many elderly and disabled  residents suffering there are so many  stories that can hurt you  this hard  worm  this terrible thing and there are many  terrible scenes to extend their reach  the volunteers launched rescue me  sponsors can read different profiles and  pick someone to rescue ensuring they'll  receive food and medicine  [Music]  many of the people receiving these  packages just aren't able to get out  this particular apartment is five floors  and the woman lives at the very top it  is hot  and she's been inside for months  of course it's important we want to eat  every day  ukraine does provide financial  assistance to elderly and disabled  people but it's not much those with  moderate disabilities f